{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-30362","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-38508","text":"TRAAVIIS — Architecture & the road to the environment surface"}]},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-30364","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-38509","marks":["bold"],"text":"Thesis."},{"id":"spn-38510","text":" TRAAVIIS is the local-first toolchain for "},{"id":"spn-38511","marks":["bold"],"text":"evidence-grade agent evaluation"},{"id":"spn-38512","text":". Not another coding agent, not a model router, not an RL cloud, not the whole TRVM research workbench. Its core loop is: "},{"id":"spn-38513","marks":["italic"],"text":"freeze the subject → run the evaluation → score explicit evidence → verify → preserve a re-verifiable receipt."},{"id":"spn-38514","text":" TRVM supplies the strongest exact-replay substrate under it; Evidence Residency is its first repository-evidence substrate.  "},{"id":"spn-38515","marks":["bold"],"text":"Write the wall. Run the world. Keep the proof."}]}],"id":"blk-30363","kind":"quote"},{"id":"blk-30365","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-38516","text":"This document describes the product boundary, what ships today, and the road to the environment surface ("},{"id":"spn-38517","marks":["code"],"text":"serve"},{"id":"spn-38518","text":"/"},{"id":"spn-38519","marks":["code"],"text":"pack"},{"id":"spn-38520","text":"/"},{"id":"spn-38521","marks":["code"],"text":"eval"},{"id":"spn-38522","text":"). It supersedes the earlier \"terminal harness engineer\" thesis — that positioning is retired."}]},{"id":"blk-30366","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-38523","text":"1. The product boundary"}]},{"id":"blk-30367","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-38524","text":"The seams are frozen on purpose. "},{"id":"spn-38525","marks":["code"],"text":"trvs"},{"id":"spn-38526","text":" carries "},{"id":"spn-38527","marks":["bold"],"text":"no substrate semantics"},{"id":"spn-38528","text":"; it packages capabilities the layers below already provide, for someone who does not know the internal history of TRVM."}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-30369","spans":[{"id":"spn-38529","text":"layer"}]},{"id":"blk-30370","spans":[{"id":"spn-38530","text":"responsibility"}]}],"id":"blk-30368","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-30371","spans":[{"id":"spn-38531","marks":["bold"],"text":"TRAAVIIS"}]},{"id":"blk-30372","spans":[{"id":"spn-38532","text":"the product — CLI, environment SDK, evaluator, packaging, visual workbench"}]}],[{"id":"blk-30373","spans":[{"id":"spn-38533","marks":["bold"],"text":"trvs"}]},{"id":"blk-30374","spans":[{"id":"spn-38534","text":"the command-line interface"}]}],[{"id":"blk-30375","spans":[{"id":"spn-38535","marks":["bold"],"text":"TaskSpecV1"}]},{"id":"blk-30376","spans":[{"id":"spn-38536","text":"the substrate-neutral assignment and evaluation contract"}]}],[{"id":"blk-30377","spans":[{"id":"spn-38537","marks":["bold"],"text":"WallRiderLang"}]},{"id":"blk-30378","spans":[{"id":"spn-38538","text":"the language for TRVM worlds, actors and world rules"}]}],[{"id":"blk-30379","spans":[{"id":"spn-38539","marks":["bold"],"text":"Forge"}]},{"id":"blk-30380","spans":[{"id":"spn-38540","text":"the compiler, identity and artifact pipeline"}]}],[{"id":"blk-30381","spans":[{"id":"spn-38541","marks":["bold"],"text":"TRVM"}]},{"id":"blk-30382","spans":[{"id":"spn-38542","text":"the deterministic execution substrate"}]}],[{"id":"blk-30383","spans":[{"id":"spn-38543","marks":["bold"],"text":"Spinner Bench"}]},{"id":"blk-30384","spans":[{"id":"spn-38544","text":"the reference workbench and conformance laboratory"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-30385","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-38545","text":"Two rules follow directly:"}]},{"id":"blk-30386","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-30388","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-38546","marks":["bold"],"text":"Spinner Bench is not TRAAVIIS."},{"id":"spn-38547","text":" It remains the place where the"}]}],"id":"blk-30387","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true},{"id":"blk-30389","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-38548","text":"language/runtime is exercised, visually inspected, and proven. TRAAVIIS "},{"id":"spn-38549","marks":["italic"],"text":"consumes"},{"id":"spn-38550","text":" those capabilities and packages them."}]},{"id":"blk-30390","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-30392","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-38551","marks":["bold"],"text":"`trvs` invents no state semantics."},{"id":"spn-38552","text":" Every command is a thin call over the"}]}],"id":"blk-30391","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":true,"start":2},{"id":"blk-30393","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-38553","text":"Forge engine's stable public API ("},{"id":"spn-38554","marks":["code"],"text":"traaviis.engine → forge_api"},{"id":"spn-38555","text":"). Identity, lowering, folding, and verification live below the CLI and are versioned there."}]},{"id":"blk-30394","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-38556","text":"2. What is real today"}]},{"id":"blk-30395","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-38557","marks":["code"],"text":"traaviis"},{"id":"spn-38558","text":" is a zero-dependency Python package exposing the "},{"id":"spn-38559","marks":["code"],"text":"trvs"},{"id":"spn-38560","text":" command over "},{"id":"spn-38561","marks":["code"],"text":"traaviis.engine"},{"id":"spn-38562","text":". Seven commands fold real worlds:"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-30397","spans":[{"id":"spn-38563","text":"command"}]},{"id":"blk-30398","spans":[{"id":"spn-38564","text":"contract"}]}],"id":"blk-30396","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-30399","spans":[{"id":"spn-38565","marks":["code"],"text":"trvs doctor"}]},{"id":"blk-30400","spans":[{"id":"spn-38566","text":"reports engine dir, API version, "},{"id":"spn-38567","marks":["code"],"text":"ic_ref"},{"id":"spn-38568","text":"/"},{"id":"spn-38569","marks":["code"],"text":"ic32"},{"id":"spn-38570","text":"/oracle status"}]}],[{"id":"blk-30401","spans":[{"id":"spn-38571","marks":["code"],"text":"trvs id"}]},{"id":"blk-30402","spans":[{"id":"spn-38572","text":"re-lowers source → "},{"id":"spn-38573","marks":["code"],"text":"SemanticArtifactID"},{"id":"spn-38574","text":" (pure identity)"}]}],[{"id":"blk-30403","spans":[{"id":"spn-38575","marks":["code"],"text":"trvs inspect"}]},{"id":"blk-30404","spans":[{"id":"spn-38576","text":"lowered actors, edges, resolved static config, diagnostics"}]}],[{"id":"blk-30405","spans":[{"id":"spn-38577","marks":["code"],"text":"trvs run"}]},{"id":"blk-30406","spans":[{"id":"spn-38578","text":"folds the world through "},{"id":"spn-38579","marks":["code"],"text":"ic_ref"},{"id":"spn-38580","text":"; prints the per-epoch film"}]}],[{"id":"blk-30407","spans":[{"id":"spn-38581","marks":["code"],"text":"trvs verify"}]},{"id":"blk-30408","spans":[{"id":"spn-38582","text":"cross-checks "},{"id":"spn-38583","marks":["code"],"text":"ic_ref"},{"id":"spn-38584","text":" vs native "},{"id":"spn-38585","marks":["code"],"text":"ic32"},{"id":"spn-38586","text":" vs the Fixture oracle"}]}],[{"id":"blk-30409","spans":[{"id":"spn-38587","marks":["code"],"text":"trvs replay"}]},{"id":"blk-30410","spans":[{"id":"spn-38588","text":"re-folds and asserts a pinned "},{"id":"spn-38589","marks":["code"],"text":"--expect"},{"id":"spn-38590","text":" id / "},{"id":"spn-38591","marks":["code"],"text":"--film"},{"id":"spn-38592","text":" hash"}]}],[{"id":"blk-30411","spans":[{"id":"spn-38593","marks":["code"],"text":"trvs diff"}]},{"id":"blk-30412","spans":[{"id":"spn-38594","text":"folds two worlds and marks the first divergent epoch"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-30413","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-38595","marks":["bold"],"text":"Identity model."},{"id":"spn-38596","text":" Presentation (position, colour, wire curve) never enters the hash; a rotor value or a rewire does. Run inputs (the scenario) are deliberately kept "},{"id":"spn-38597","marks":["italic"],"text":"out"},{"id":"spn-38598","text":" of the "},{"id":"spn-38599","marks":["code"],"text":"SemanticArtifactID"},{"id":"spn-38600","text":" and carried as a separate "},{"id":"spn-38601","marks":["code"],"text":"scen-…"},{"id":"spn-38602","text":" digest. This is the split that makes an environment content-addressable."}]},{"id":"blk-30414","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-38603","marks":["bold"],"text":"Verification contract."},{"id":"spn-38604","text":" A film is not asserted — it is "},{"id":"spn-38605","marks":["italic"],"text":"checked by every applicable verifier"},{"id":"spn-38606","text":". The reference reducer ("},{"id":"spn-38607","marks":["code"],"text":"ic_ref"},{"id":"spn-38608","text":"), the compiled native reducer ("},{"id":"spn-38609","marks":["code"],"text":"ic32"},{"id":"spn-38610","text":"), and an independent oracle each run where their domain applies and must agree byte-for-byte. Coverage is explicit: a verifier that cannot apply to a world is reported "},{"id":"spn-38611","marks":["code"],"text":"not_applicable"},{"id":"spn-38612","text":", never counted as a pass or a fail. The Golden Spinner agrees 3/3; a bare Blank Spinner is a valid world for "},{"id":"spn-38613","marks":["code"],"text":"ic_ref == ic32"},{"id":"spn-38614","text":" but sits outside the Fixture oracle's domain. Exit codes: "},{"id":"spn-38615","marks":["code"],"text":"0"},{"id":"spn-38616","text":" agree, "},{"id":"spn-38617","marks":["code"],"text":"1"},{"id":"spn-38618","text":" ran-and-disagreed, "},{"id":"spn-38619","marks":["code"],"text":"2"},{"id":"spn-38620","text":" a verifier was unavailable. That makes any verifying command a fail-closed gate."}]},{"id":"blk-30415","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-38621","text":"3. The environment surface (roadmap)"}]},{"id":"blk-30416","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-38622","text":"The gap between \"a verifiable world\" and \"an environment an agent trains against\" is task/reward/episode lifecycle. The internal contract for that lifecycle is a "},{"id":"spn-38623","marks":["bold"],"text":"neutral Episode Kernel"},{"id":"spn-38624","text":" — public protocols are "},{"id":"spn-38625","marks":["italic"],"text":"adapters"},{"id":"spn-38626","text":" over it, never runtime law. This keeps "},{"id":"spn-38627","marks":[{"kind":"link","predicate":"cites","target":"https://openreward.ai"}],"text":"Open Reward Standard"},{"id":"spn-38628","text":" or MCP evolution from ever becoming TRVM runtime semantics."}]},{"id":"blk-30417","kind":"code","language":"text","text":"Episode Kernel   start · observe · step · reset · finalize   (internal, neutral)\n        ↓\nORS adapter      first / primary public surface  →  trvs serve --ors\nMCP adapter      compatibility (tools/resources/prompts)  →  trvs serve --mcp\nJSONL adapter    local automation / debugging"},{"id":"blk-30418","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-38629","text":"The kernel carries "},{"id":"spn-38630","marks":["bold"],"text":"no substrate semantics"},{"id":"spn-38631","text":"; each verb is substrate-defined and may be declared "},{"id":"spn-38632","marks":["italic"],"text":"unsupported"},{"id":"spn-38633","text":" rather than faked. "},{"id":"spn-38634","marks":["code"],"text":"start"},{"id":"spn-38635","text":" prepares the frozen subject; "},{"id":"spn-38636","marks":["code"],"text":"finalize"},{"id":"spn-38637","text":" seals the trace and outputs, runs the verifier plan, scores the reward, and emits the episode. "},{"id":"spn-38638","marks":["code"],"text":"observe"},{"id":"spn-38639","text":" / "},{"id":"spn-38640","marks":["code"],"text":"step"},{"id":"spn-38641","text":" / "},{"id":"spn-38642","marks":["code"],"text":"reset"},{"id":"spn-38643","text":" are supported only where a substrate can honour them — "},{"id":"spn-38644","marks":["bold"],"text":"Evidence Residency v1 is one-shot and implements only `start → finalize`."},{"id":"spn-38645","text":" For the TRVM profile, "},{"id":"spn-38646","marks":["code"],"text":"observe"},{"id":"spn-38647","text":" is a label-free "},{"id":"spn-38648","marks":["code"],"text":"_digest_domain"},{"id":"spn-38649","text":" projection, "},{"id":"spn-38650","marks":["code"],"text":"step"},{"id":"spn-38651","text":" extends the epoch-input stream, "},{"id":"spn-38652","marks":["code"],"text":"reset"},{"id":"spn-38653","text":" reconstructs "},{"id":"spn-38654","marks":["code"],"text":"sem-… + scen-…"},{"id":"spn-38655","text":" at epoch 0, and "},{"id":"spn-38656","marks":["code"],"text":"finalize"},{"id":"spn-38657","text":" checks "},{"id":"spn-38658","marks":["code"],"text":"ic_ref == ic32 == oracle"},{"id":"spn-38659","text":"; those are TRVM profile bindings, not kernel law. The ORS wire surface ("},{"id":"spn-38660","marks":["code"],"text":"list_tasks · session · call_tool → reward · finished"},{"id":"spn-38661","text":") and the MCP primitives ("},{"id":"spn-38662","marks":["code"],"text":"tools · resources · prompts"},{"id":"spn-38663","text":") are both "},{"id":"spn-38664","marks":["italic"],"text":"projections"},{"id":"spn-38665","text":" of the same kernel. The kernel owns the semantics; adapters only translate."}]},{"id":"blk-30419","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-38666","text":"3a. The artifact ladder"}]},{"id":"blk-30420","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-38667","text":"TRAAVIIS freezes a "},{"id":"spn-38668","marks":["bold"],"text":"substrate-neutral"},{"id":"spn-38669","text":" artifact ladder. The lowest rung is the "},{"id":"spn-38670","marks":["italic"],"text":"substrate subject"},{"id":"spn-38671","text":", sealed differently by each substrate; every rung above it is shared, so two researchers never argue about what agreed and what did not:"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-30422","spans":[{"id":"spn-38672","text":"id / rung"}]},{"id":"blk-30423","spans":[{"id":"spn-38673","text":"question"}]},{"id":"blk-30424","spans":[{"id":"spn-38674","text":"domain"}]}],"id":"blk-30421","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-30425","spans":[{"id":"spn-38675","marks":["bold"],"text":"substrate subject"}]},{"id":"blk-30426","spans":[{"id":"spn-38676","text":"was it the same subject?"}]},{"id":"blk-30427","spans":[{"id":"spn-38677","text":"TRVM: "},{"id":"spn-38678","marks":["code"],"text":"sem-…"},{"id":"spn-38679","text":"+"},{"id":"spn-38680","marks":["code"],"text":"scen-…"},{"id":"spn-38681","text":" · Residency: "},{"id":"spn-38682","marks":["code"],"text":"snap-…"}]}],[{"id":"blk-30428","spans":[{"id":"spn-38683","marks":["code"],"text":"rew-…"}]},{"id":"blk-30429","spans":[{"id":"spn-38684","text":"same scoring rubric?"}]},{"id":"blk-30430","spans":[{"id":"spn-38685","text":"declared reward spec"}]}],[{"id":"blk-30431","spans":[{"id":"spn-38686","marks":["code"],"text":"task-…"}]},{"id":"blk-30432","spans":[{"id":"spn-38687","text":"same assignment?"}]},{"id":"blk-30433","spans":[{"id":"spn-38688","text":"subject + reward + terminate"}]}],[{"id":"blk-30434","spans":[{"id":"spn-38689","marks":["code"],"text":"trace-…"}]},{"id":"blk-30435","spans":[{"id":"spn-38690","text":"same observable behavior?"}]},{"id":"blk-30436","spans":[{"id":"spn-38691","text":"the recorded observable record"}]}],[{"id":"blk-30437","spans":[{"id":"spn-38692","marks":["code"],"text":"episode-…"}]},{"id":"blk-30438","spans":[{"id":"spn-38693","text":"same evaluated outcome?"}]},{"id":"blk-30439","spans":[{"id":"spn-38694","text":"trace + rubric → receipt"}]}],[{"id":"blk-30440","spans":[{"id":"spn-38695","marks":["code"],"text":"env-…"}]},{"id":"blk-30441","spans":[{"id":"spn-38696","text":"same environment release?"}]},{"id":"blk-30442","spans":[{"id":"spn-38697","text":"subject + tasks + rewards + splits"}]}],[{"id":"blk-30443","spans":[{"id":"spn-38698","marks":["code"],"text":"bundle-…"}]},{"id":"blk-30444","spans":[{"id":"spn-38699","text":"same distributed package?"}]},{"id":"blk-30445","spans":[{"id":"spn-38700","text":"env + presentation + docs"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-30446","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-38701","text":"The shared evaluation constructs ("},{"id":"spn-38702","marks":["code"],"text":"task-…"},{"id":"spn-38703","text":", "},{"id":"spn-38704","marks":["code"],"text":"rew-…"},{"id":"spn-38705","text":", "},{"id":"spn-38706","marks":["code"],"text":"episode-…"},{"id":"spn-38707","text":", the substrate profile) live in the "},{"id":"spn-38708","marks":["code"],"text":"traaviis.*"},{"id":"spn-38709","text":" namespace; substrate-specific evidence lives below. "},{"id":"spn-38710","marks":["code"],"text":"sem-…"},{"id":"spn-38711","text":"/"},{"id":"spn-38712","marks":["code"],"text":"scen-…"},{"id":"spn-38713","text":" are "},{"id":"spn-38714","marks":["bold"],"text":"TRVM substrate identities"},{"id":"spn-38715","text":", not universal rungs; "},{"id":"spn-38716","marks":["code"],"text":"snap-…"},{"id":"spn-38717","text":" is the Residency subject. A "},{"id":"spn-38718","marks":["bold"],"text":"`trace-…`"},{"id":"spn-38719","text":" is the substrate-neutral observable record; a "},{"id":"spn-38720","marks":["bold"],"text":"`film-…`"},{"id":"spn-38721","text":" is the "},{"id":"spn-38722","marks":["italic"],"text":"TRVM case"},{"id":"spn-38723","text":" of a "},{"id":"spn-38724","marks":["code"],"text":"trace-…"},{"id":"spn-38725","text":" — a deterministic-execution artifact that does not generalize. Forge owns TRVM compilation and identity ("},{"id":"spn-38726","marks":["code"],"text":"sem-…"},{"id":"spn-38727","text":"/"},{"id":"spn-38728","marks":["code"],"text":"scen-…"},{"id":"spn-38729","text":"/"},{"id":"spn-38730","marks":["code"],"text":"film-…"},{"id":"spn-38731","text":"); TRAAVIIS owns the shared evaluation ladder."}]},{"id":"blk-30447","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-38732","text":"Re-scoring the "},{"id":"spn-38733","marks":["italic"],"text":"same"},{"id":"spn-38734","text":" trace under a different rubric changes the "},{"id":"spn-38735","marks":["code"],"text":"episode-…"},{"id":"spn-38736","text":" receipt but never the "},{"id":"spn-38737","marks":["code"],"text":"trace-…"},{"id":"spn-38738","text":" — the recorded behavior did not change."}]},{"id":"blk-30448","kind":"heading","level":4,"spans":[{"id":"spn-38739","text":"Canonical form (what an id is a hash "},{"id":"spn-38740","marks":["italic"],"text":"of"},{"id":"spn-38741","text":")"}]},{"id":"blk-30449","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-38742","text":"Every rung is "},{"id":"spn-38743","marks":["code"],"text":"<prefix>-<sha256(canonical_bytes(document))>"},{"id":"spn-38744","text":", where "},{"id":"spn-38745","marks":["code"],"text":"canonical_bytes"},{"id":"spn-38746","text":" is "},{"id":"spn-38747","marks":["bold"],"text":"TRAAVIIS canonical JSON"},{"id":"spn-38748","text":": UTF-8, object keys sorted, no insignificant whitespace — concretely "},{"id":"spn-38749","marks":["code"],"text":"json.dumps(obj, sort_keys=True, separators=(\",\", \":\"), ensure_ascii=False)"},{"id":"spn-38750","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-30450","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-38751","text":"This is "},{"id":"spn-38752","marks":["italic"],"text":"not"},{"id":"spn-38753","text":" RFC 8785 (JCS), and the difference is stated here rather than discovered by a reimplementer. It is byte-identical to RFC 8785 over documents whose keys hold no code point at or above U+10000 and whose numbers avoid four bands, but it differs in two ways that are already reachable:"}]},{"id":"blk-30451","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-30453","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-38754","marks":["bold"],"text":"Numbers."},{"id":"spn-38755","text":" RFC 8785 mandates ECMAScript "},{"id":"spn-38756","marks":["code"],"text":"Number::toString"},{"id":"spn-38757","text":"; Python does not"}]}],"id":"blk-30452","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-30454","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-38758","text":"match it for integral-valued floats below 10²¹ ("},{"id":"spn-38759","marks":["code"],"text":"1.0"},{"id":"spn-38760","text":" vs "},{"id":"spn-38761","marks":["code"],"text":"1"},{"id":"spn-38762","text":"), for "},{"id":"spn-38763","marks":["code"],"text":"-0.0"},{"id":"spn-38764","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-38765","marks":["code"],"text":"-0.0"},{"id":"spn-38766","text":" vs "},{"id":"spn-38767","marks":["code"],"text":"0"},{"id":"spn-38768","text":"), across "},{"id":"spn-38769","marks":["code"],"text":"[1e16, 1e21)"},{"id":"spn-38770","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-38771","marks":["code"],"text":"[1e-6, 1e-4)"},{"id":"spn-38772","text":", or on exponent zero-padding ("},{"id":"spn-38773","marks":["code"],"text":"1e-07"},{"id":"spn-38774","text":" vs "},{"id":"spn-38775","marks":["code"],"text":"1e-7"},{"id":"spn-38776","text":"). A receipt's "},{"id":"spn-38777","marks":["code"],"text":"reward"},{"id":"spn-38778","text":" is always a float, so a fully-passing episode carries "},{"id":"spn-38779","marks":["code"],"text":"1.0"},{"id":"spn-38780","text":" and is on the diverging side."}]},{"id":"blk-30455","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-30457","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-38781","marks":["bold"],"text":"Key order."},{"id":"spn-38782","text":" RFC 8785 sorts property names by UTF-16 code unit; Python sorts"}]}],"id":"blk-30456","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-30458","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-38783","text":"by code point. These agree below U+10000 and diverge above it, so a subject repository containing an astral-plane filename orders its "},{"id":"spn-38784","marks":["code"],"text":"files"},{"id":"spn-38785","text":" map differently under the two schemes."}]},{"id":"blk-30459","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-38786","text":"Nothing enforces the agreeing subset — there is no schema check, key charset check or numeric domain check anywhere on the path. "},{"id":"spn-38787","marks":["code"],"text":"test/test_canonical.py"},{"id":"spn-38788","text":" measures all of this against a reference RFC 8785 implementation and pins each divergence with a reproducing value; treat it as the specification of the canonical form until a ruling decides whether to conform and migrate."}]},{"id":"blk-30460","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-38789","text":"3b. The bundle — "},{"id":"spn-38790","marks":["code"],"text":"traaviis.environment.v1"}]},{"id":"blk-30461","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-38791","marks":["code"],"text":"trvs pack"},{"id":"spn-38792","text":" separates "},{"id":"spn-38793","marks":["italic"],"text":"what an environment means"},{"id":"spn-38794","text":" from "},{"id":"spn-38795","marks":["italic"],"text":"how it is shipped"},{"id":"spn-38796","text":". The "},{"id":"spn-38797","marks":["bold"],"text":"environment manifest"},{"id":"spn-38798","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-38799","marks":["code"],"text":"env-…"},{"id":"spn-38800","text":") fixes the substrate subject, tasks, rewards, action / observation or verifier profiles, and split membership; the outer "},{"id":"spn-38801","marks":["bold"],"text":"package"},{"id":"spn-38802","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-38803","marks":["code"],"text":"bundle-…"},{"id":"spn-38804","text":") carries presentation, docs, and screenshots and may change without moving "},{"id":"spn-38805","marks":["code"],"text":"env-…"},{"id":"spn-38806","text":". For the TRVM substrate it layers over the existing "},{"id":"spn-38807","marks":["code"],"text":"forge.bundle.v2"},{"id":"spn-38808","text":" (world + scenarios, already closed), adding "},{"id":"spn-38809","marks":["code"],"text":"{tasks, rewards, splits, profiles}"},{"id":"spn-38810","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-30462","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-38811","marks":["code"],"text":"pack"},{"id":"spn-38812","text":" runs against a "},{"id":"spn-38813","marks":["bold"],"text":"substrate-profile admission interface"},{"id":"spn-38814","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-38815","marks":["code"],"text":"validate_subject · verify_closure · recompute_subject_identity · reopen_package"},{"id":"spn-38816","text":"), not against "},{"id":"spn-38817","marks":["code"],"text":"world"},{"id":"spn-38818","text":" verbs; each substrate implements it (TRVM re-lowers source → "},{"id":"spn-38819","marks":["code"],"text":"sem-…"},{"id":"spn-38820","text":"; Residency recomputes snapshot → "},{"id":"spn-38821","marks":["code"],"text":"snap-…"},{"id":"spn-38822","text":"). Three laws (mirroring the existing Forge bundle discipline):"}]},{"id":"blk-30463","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-30465","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-38823","marks":["bold"],"text":"self-sufficiency"},{"id":"spn-38824","text":" — the object set is derived from the doc."}]}],"id":"blk-30464","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-30467","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-38825","marks":["bold"],"text":"closure"},{"id":"spn-38826","text":" — the subject re-derives to its declared identity and every task /"}]}],"id":"blk-30466","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-30468","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-38827","text":"reward / subject reference resolves inside the closure, or import fails loudly."}]},{"id":"blk-30469","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-30471","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-38828","marks":["bold"],"text":"identity"},{"id":"spn-38829","text":" — "},{"id":"spn-38830","marks":["code"],"text":"pack"},{"id":"spn-38831","text":" re-opens and re-verifies the emitted bundle before"}]}],"id":"blk-30470","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-30472","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-38832","text":"reporting success."}]},{"id":"blk-30473","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-38833","marks":["bold"],"text":"Shipped"},{"id":"spn-38834","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-38835","marks":["code"],"text":"traaviis/substrates.py"},{"id":"spn-38836","text":", "},{"id":"spn-38837","marks":["code"],"text":"traaviis/pack.py"},{"id":"spn-38838","text":", "},{"id":"spn-38839","marks":["code"],"text":"traaviis/scaffold.py"},{"id":"spn-38840","text":"). "},{"id":"spn-38841","marks":["code"],"text":"init"},{"id":"spn-38842","text":" scaffolds and derives nothing — it emits scaffold-level references ("},{"id":"spn-38843","marks":["code"],"text":"reward_spec"},{"id":"spn-38844","text":", "},{"id":"spn-38845","marks":["code"],"text":"snapshot_def"},{"id":"spn-38846","text":") precisely so it never asserts a hash it did not compute — and "},{"id":"spn-38847","marks":["code"],"text":"pack"},{"id":"spn-38848","text":" replaces them with recomputed ids. "},{"id":"spn-38849","marks":["code"],"text":"env-…"},{"id":"spn-38850","text":" is derived from an explicit identity allowlist ("},{"id":"spn-38851","marks":["code"],"text":"substrate_profile · subject · tasks · rewards · profiles · splits"},{"id":"spn-38852","text":"), so renaming an environment or rewriting its description moves the "},{"id":"spn-38853","marks":["italic"],"text":"package"},{"id":"spn-38854","text":", never "},{"id":"spn-38855","marks":["code"],"text":"env-…"},{"id":"spn-38856","text":". Both substrate profiles are implemented; a single-task residency package is emitted as a runnable eval-bundle, closing "},{"id":"spn-38857","marks":["code"],"text":"init → pack → eval-one"},{"id":"spn-38858","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-30474","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-38859","text":"An episode emits a receipt:"}]},{"id":"blk-30475","kind":"code","language":"json","text":"{ \"episode_version\": \"traaviis.episode.v1\", \"substrate_profile\": \"trvm.world.v1\",\n  \"task_id\": \"task-…\", \"subject\": { \"world\": \"sem-…\", \"scenario\": \"scen-…\" },\n  \"reward_id\": \"rew-…\", \"trace\": \"film-…\", \"episode_id\": \"episode-…\",\n  \"reward\": 1, \"status\": \"ok\", \"finished\": true,\n  \"verification\": { \"reference\": \"pass\", \"native\": \"pass\", \"oracle\": \"not_applicable\" } }"},{"id":"blk-30476","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-38860","text":"For a Residency episode the same receipt carries "},{"id":"spn-38861","marks":["code"],"text":"\"substrate_profile\": \"residency.repository.v1\""},{"id":"spn-38862","text":", a "},{"id":"spn-38863","marks":["code"],"text":"trace-…"},{"id":"spn-38864","text":" in place of the "},{"id":"spn-38865","marks":["code"],"text":"film-…"},{"id":"spn-38866","text":", and "},{"id":"spn-38867","marks":["code"],"text":"citations"},{"id":"spn-38868","text":"/"},{"id":"spn-38869","marks":["code"],"text":"patch"},{"id":"spn-38870","text":"/"},{"id":"spn-38871","marks":["code"],"text":"tests"},{"id":"spn-38872","text":"/"},{"id":"spn-38873","marks":["code"],"text":"identity"},{"id":"spn-38874","text":" verifier fields. Every verifier field is one of "},{"id":"spn-38875","marks":["code"],"text":"pass"},{"id":"spn-38876","text":", "},{"id":"spn-38877","marks":["code"],"text":"fail"},{"id":"spn-38878","text":", "},{"id":"spn-38879","marks":["code"],"text":"not_applicable"},{"id":"spn-38880","text":", or "},{"id":"spn-38881","marks":["code"],"text":"error"},{"id":"spn-38882","text":" — coverage is never silently dropped, and "},{"id":"spn-38883","marks":["code"],"text":"error"},{"id":"spn-38884","text":" (substrate unavailable) stays distinct from "},{"id":"spn-38885","marks":["code"],"text":"fail"},{"id":"spn-38886","text":" (the work was wrong)."}]},{"id":"blk-30477","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-38887","text":"3c. Evaluation before training"}]},{"id":"blk-30478","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-38888","text":"The first job is not a trainer, and the first interface is not a batch. It is a one-shot "},{"id":"spn-38889","marks":["bold"],"text":"`trvs eval-one task.json --agent-command …`"},{"id":"spn-38890","text":" over a single frozen subject. Batch "},{"id":"spn-38891","marks":["code"],"text":"trvs eval"},{"id":"spn-38892","text":" follows once eval-one is boring. Because every episode is verified and content-addressed, the numbers are reproducible and the traces are re-checkable. Training frameworks drive rollouts "},{"id":"spn-38893","marks":["italic"],"text":"through"},{"id":"spn-38894","text":" the ORS adapter later."}]},{"id":"blk-30479","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-38895","marks":["bold"],"text":"Shipped"},{"id":"spn-38896","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-38897","marks":["code"],"text":"traaviis/evalsplit.py"},{"id":"spn-38898","text":"). "},{"id":"spn-38899","marks":["code"],"text":"trvs eval PKG --split NAME"},{"id":"spn-38900","text":" runs an agent over a split and emits one "},{"id":"spn-38901","marks":["code"],"text":"episode-…"},{"id":"spn-38902","text":" per task. It adds "},{"id":"spn-38903","marks":["bold"],"text":"no rung to the ladder"},{"id":"spn-38904","text":" — §1 stops at "},{"id":"spn-38905","marks":["code"],"text":"env-…"},{"id":"spn-38906","text":"/"},{"id":"spn-38907","marks":["code"],"text":"bundle-…"},{"id":"spn-38908","text":", so a run over a split gets an "},{"id":"spn-38909","marks":["italic"],"text":"index"},{"id":"spn-38910","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-38911","marks":["code"],"text":"traaviis.evaluation.v1"},{"id":"spn-38912","text":") naming the "},{"id":"spn-38913","marks":["code"],"text":"env-…"},{"id":"spn-38914","text":", the split, and the episode ids, and carries no id of its own. The admission order mirrors "},{"id":"spn-38915","marks":["code"],"text":"pack"},{"id":"spn-38916","text":": reopen the package (every id re-derived from the written bytes) → resolve the split → bind the subject tree to its snapshot → "},{"id":"spn-38917","marks":["italic"],"text":"only then"},{"id":"spn-38918","text":" launch anything. A task that fails is recorded as a failed episode and the split continues; a refusal exits 2 rather than reporting a score of zero."}]},{"id":"blk-30480","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-38919","marks":["italic"],"text":"Canonical form."},{"id":"spn-38920","text":" An environment is a closed "},{"id":"spn-38921","marks":["bold"],"text":"set"},{"id":"spn-38922","text":" of tasks, rewards and split members (§3), and a set has exactly one written order — so "},{"id":"spn-38923","marks":["code"],"text":"pack"},{"id":"spn-38924","text":" sorts tasks and rewards by their derived ids and split members by task id, and reordering an author's source list moves no identity. Producing that order is not enough: "},{"id":"spn-38925","marks":["code"],"text":"open_package"},{"id":"spn-38926","text":" "},{"id":"spn-38927","marks":["bold"],"text":"re-checks"},{"id":"spn-38928","text":" it, because a hand-built manifest that is internally consistent but unsorted would otherwise reopen cleanly and give one environment as many identities as its task list has permutations. A noncanonical manifest is "},{"id":"spn-38929","marks":["code"],"text":"MANIFEST_NONCANONICAL"},{"id":"spn-38930","text":", checked before the "},{"id":"spn-38931","marks":["code"],"text":"env-…"},{"id":"spn-38932","text":" comparison so the failure reads as a malformed "},{"id":"spn-38933","marks":["italic"],"text":"form"},{"id":"spn-38934","text":" rather than a confusing identity mismatch."}]},{"id":"blk-30481","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-38935","marks":["italic"],"text":"Two outcomes, not one."},{"id":"spn-38936","text":" Each index entry carries "},{"id":"spn-38937","marks":["code"],"text":"status"},{"id":"spn-38938","text":"/"},{"id":"spn-38939","marks":["code"],"text":"reward"},{"id":"spn-38940","text":" — what the evaluation found — and a separate "},{"id":"spn-38941","marks":["code"],"text":"persistence {requested, status, error}"},{"id":"spn-38942","text":" — whether the evidence the caller asked to keep was kept. Conflating them once let a run report "},{"id":"spn-38943","marks":["code"],"text":"ok"},{"id":"spn-38944","text":" for an episode whose bundle had failed to write: a score with no retained proof, reported as if the proof existed. The totals count both, and the exit code reads them in precedence — persistence failure 2, disagreement 1, otherwise 0. "},{"id":"spn-38945","marks":["code"],"text":"OSError"},{"id":"spn-38946","text":" is caught alongside "},{"id":"spn-38947","marks":["code"],"text":"EpisodeBundleError"},{"id":"spn-38948","text":" deliberately: a read-only output directory is the most ordinary way retention fails, and it must be a recorded outcome for one task rather than an exception that abandons the rest of the split."}]},{"id":"blk-30482","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-38949","text":"3c-bis. Verifier wiring — "},{"id":"spn-38950","marks":["code"],"text":"VerifierRegistryV1"}]},{"id":"blk-30483","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-38951","text":"Three things that are easy to conflate are kept distinct:"}]},{"head":[{"id":"blk-30485","spans":[{"id":"spn-38952","text":"layer"}]},{"id":"blk-30486","spans":[{"id":"spn-38953","text":"function of"}]},{"id":"blk-30487","spans":[{"id":"spn-38954","text":"where it lives"}]}],"id":"blk-30484","kind":"table","rows":[[{"id":"blk-30488","spans":[{"id":"spn-38955","text":"declared plan"}]},{"id":"blk-30489","spans":[{"id":"spn-38956","text":"the task alone"}]},{"id":"blk-30490","spans":[{"id":"spn-38957","marks":["code"],"text":"wiring.declared_signals"}]}],[{"id":"blk-30491","spans":[{"id":"spn-38958","text":"available implementations"}]},{"id":"blk-30492","spans":[{"id":"spn-38959","text":"task + runtime/registry"}]},{"id":"blk-30493","spans":[{"id":"spn-38960","marks":["code"],"text":"VerifierRegistryV1"}]}],[{"id":"blk-30494","spans":[{"id":"spn-38961","text":"sealed history"}]},{"id":"blk-30495","spans":[{"id":"spn-38962","text":"what actually answered"}]},{"id":"blk-30496","spans":[{"id":"spn-38963","marks":["code"],"text":"receipt.verifier_versions"}]}]]},{"id":"blk-30497","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-38964","text":"The registry is built "},{"id":"spn-38965","marks":["bold"],"text":"once per command"},{"id":"spn-38966","text":" from the engine that command selected, so every task in a split is answered by the same verifiers bound to the same Forge checkout — and "},{"id":"spn-38967","marks":["code"],"text":"real_adapter(forge_api)"},{"id":"spn-38968","text":" takes that engine explicitly rather than independently rediscovering a possibly different one. An unreachable engine leaves "},{"id":"spn-38969","marks":["code"],"text":"identity"},{"id":"spn-38970","text":" declared but unwired, reported as a note; it is never silently dropped and never faked into a "},{"id":"spn-38971","marks":["code"],"text":"pass"},{"id":"spn-38972","text":". Because the versions are sealed into "},{"id":"spn-38973","marks":["code"],"text":"episode-…"},{"id":"spn-38974","text":", an engine upgrade honestly moves the episode id instead of quietly re-scoring the same one."}]},{"id":"blk-30498","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-38975","text":"3c-ter. Test plans — "},{"id":"spn-38976","marks":["code"],"text":"traaviis.test-plan.v2"}]},{"id":"blk-30499","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-38977","text":"V2 replaced host-specific "},{"id":"spn-38978","marks":["code"],"text":"argv"},{"id":"spn-38979","text":" with a logical "},{"id":"spn-38980","marks":["code"],"text":"tool"},{"id":"spn-38981","text":" + "},{"id":"spn-38982","marks":["code"],"text":"args"},{"id":"spn-38983","text":" under a named "},{"id":"spn-38984","marks":["code"],"text":"toolchain_profile"},{"id":"spn-38985","text":", so "},{"id":"spn-38986","marks":["code"],"text":"task-…"},{"id":"spn-38987","text":" is host-independent and the resolved binary is an execution fact. It further lets each command declare per-phase "},{"id":"spn-38988","marks":["code"],"text":"allowed_exit_codes"},{"id":"spn-38989","text":", both defaulting to "},{"id":"spn-38990","marks":["code"],"text":"[0]"},{"id":"spn-38991","text":" — exactly the V1 rule, so an undeclared plan keeps its old meaning. This is what makes a "},{"id":"spn-38992","marks":["bold"],"text":"repair task"},{"id":"spn-38993","text":" expressible: under a hardcoded baseline-must-exit-0 rule, a task could not require a test that fails before the fix and passes after, which is the ordinary shape of a real bug report. The verdict asymmetry is deliberate — the baseline judges the "},{"id":"spn-38994","marks":["italic"],"text":"fixture"},{"id":"spn-38995","text":" (a miss is "},{"id":"spn-38996","marks":["code"],"text":"error"},{"id":"spn-38997","text":", the task is inadmissible), the patched run judges the "},{"id":"spn-38998","marks":["italic"],"text":"candidate"},{"id":"spn-38999","text":" (a miss is "},{"id":"spn-39000","marks":["code"],"text":"fail"},{"id":"spn-39001","text":") — and every record states the "},{"id":"spn-39002","marks":["code"],"text":"expected_exit_codes"},{"id":"spn-39003","text":" it was judged by, so the evidence names its own rule."}]},{"id":"blk-30500","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-39004","text":"3d. Later: verified process rewards"}]},{"id":"blk-30501","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-39005","text":"Because TRVM films observe each transition, TRAAVIIS can eventually emit intermediate, verifier-grounded rewards (e.g. "},{"id":"spn-39006","marks":["code"],"text":"+0.2 preserved safety invariant"},{"id":"spn-39007","text":", "},{"id":"spn-39008","marks":["code"],"text":"-0.3 duplicated forbidden resource"},{"id":"spn-39009","text":") rather than only a terminal reward. This depends entirely on verifier reliability, so it ships "},{"id":"spn-39010","marks":["bold"],"text":"after"},{"id":"spn-39011","text":" deterministic terminal rewards and complete episodes are solid."}]},{"id":"blk-30502","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-39012","text":"4. Sequencing"}]},{"id":"blk-30503","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-39013","text":"The thesis is "},{"id":"spn-39014","marks":["bold"],"text":"evidence-grade environments for evaluating agents"},{"id":"spn-39015","text":". The sequencing builds "},{"id":"spn-39016","marks":["italic"],"text":"one"},{"id":"spn-39017","text":" end-to-end evaluation environment before widening the platform. Flagship worlds ship in this order:"}]},{"id":"blk-30504","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-39018","marks":["bold"],"text":"Golden Spinner → Evidence Residency → Courier → WallRider."}]},{"id":"blk-30505","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-30507","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-39019","marks":["bold"],"text":"v0.7-5 (Spinner Bench)"},{"id":"spn-39020","text":" — close the Public Alpha: freeze presentation,"}]}],"id":"blk-30506","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-30508","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-39021","text":"package source, document limits, publish reproducible acceptance. Then freeze Bench feature work. Bench proceeds "},{"id":"spn-39022","marks":["italic"],"text":"independently"},{"id":"spn-39023","text":" and does not block the evaluation surface below."}]},{"id":"blk-30509","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-30511","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-39024","marks":["bold"],"text":"TRAAVIIS v0.1"},{"id":"spn-39025","text":" — the shared artifact ladder as pure identity functions"}]}],"id":"blk-30510","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-30512","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-39026","text":"("},{"id":"spn-39027","marks":["code"],"text":"snapshot_id · finding_id · patch_id · trace_id · reward_id · task_id · episode_id"},{"id":"spn-39028","text":") with mutation-law tests, then "},{"id":"spn-39029","marks":["code"],"text":"trvs eval-one"},{"id":"spn-39030","text":" over "},{"id":"spn-39031","marks":["bold"],"text":"Evidence Residency"},{"id":"spn-39032","text":" — an agent inspects a frozen repository, finds a real spec/impl inconsistency, cites evidence, proposes the smallest patch, runs the declared checks, and returns a structured finding + a re-verifiable receipt. Ship Golden Spinner as the first TRVM bundle alongside. See "},{"id":"spn-39033","marks":["code"],"text":"RFC_EVIDENCE_RESIDENCY.md"},{"id":"spn-39034","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-30513","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-30515","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-39035","marks":["bold"],"text":"TRAAVIIS v0.2"},{"id":"spn-39036","text":" — the Episode Kernel + "},{"id":"spn-39037","marks":["code"],"text":"trvs serve --ors"},{"id":"spn-39038","text":"; ship the"}]}],"id":"blk-30514","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-30516","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-39039","marks":["bold"],"text":"Courier"},{"id":"spn-39040","text":"/Factory world so the kernel is exercised by a stateful, long-horizon environment "},{"id":"spn-39041","marks":["italic"],"text":"before"},{"id":"spn-39042","text":" batch "},{"id":"spn-39043","marks":["code"],"text":"eval"},{"id":"spn-39044","text":" is called complete."}]},{"id":"blk-30517","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-30519","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-39045","marks":["bold"],"text":"TRAAVIIS v0.3"},{"id":"spn-39046","text":" — batch "},{"id":"spn-39047","marks":["code"],"text":"eval · compare · reports"},{"id":"spn-39048","text":" over the kernel; MCP"}]}],"id":"blk-30518","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-30520","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-39049","text":"adapter."}]},{"id":"blk-30521","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-30523","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-39050","marks":["bold"],"text":"TRAAVIIS v0.4"},{"id":"spn-39051","text":" — an ORS/TRL example, process-reward hooks, environment"}]}],"id":"blk-30522","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-30524","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-39052","text":"publishing; ship the "},{"id":"spn-39053","marks":["bold"],"text":"WallRider"},{"id":"spn-39054","text":"/Graffiti world."}]},{"id":"blk-30525","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-39055","text":"5. What is deliberately not built"}]},{"id":"blk-30526","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-39056","text":"Model routing · generic sub-agent orchestration · another chat interface · a cloud GPU training service · a giant environment marketplace · a complete game engine · plugin systems before the bundle/session API is stable · a complex interactive REPL · automatic LLM world generation as the core proposition."}]},{"id":"blk-30527","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-39057","text":"LLM-assisted authoring ("},{"id":"spn-39058","marks":["code"],"text":"trvs propose \"add a locked gate opened by two signals\""},{"id":"spn-39059","text":") can be useful later — but the model must produce a "},{"id":"spn-39060","marks":["italic"],"text":"reviewable graph edit"},{"id":"spn-39061","text":", and the deterministic system stays authoritative."}]},{"id":"blk-30528","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-39062","text":"6. The environment RFC (rulings received)"}]},{"id":"blk-30529","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-39063","text":"The environment surface introduces genuinely new semantic/runtime constructs. Those were ruled below "},{"id":"spn-39064","marks":["code"],"text":"trvs"},{"id":"spn-39065","text":", not invented in it. The rulings — reward as a first-class "},{"id":"spn-39066","marks":["code"],"text":"rew-…"},{"id":"spn-39067","text":" artifact, tasks as first-class with splits as manifest sets, "},{"id":"spn-39068","marks":["code"],"text":"env-…"},{"id":"spn-39069","text":" vs "},{"id":"spn-39070","marks":["code"],"text":"bundle-…"},{"id":"spn-39071","text":", the episode/reset/replay contract ("},{"id":"spn-39072","marks":["code"],"text":"reset"},{"id":"spn-39073","text":" reconstructs initial state, "},{"id":"spn-39074","marks":["code"],"text":"replay"},{"id":"spn-39075","text":" reapplies a recorded action stream — they are "},{"id":"spn-39076","marks":["italic"],"text":"not"},{"id":"spn-39077","text":" the same), one server / many sessions with no global lock, and "},{"id":"spn-39078","marks":["code"],"text":"init"},{"id":"spn-39079","text":"/"},{"id":"spn-39080","marks":["code"],"text":"pack"},{"id":"spn-39081","text":" admission laws — are captured in "},{"id":"spn-39082","marks":["code"],"text":"RFC_TRAAVIIS_ARTIFACTS.md"},{"id":"spn-39083","text":", together with the mutation laws each construct must satisfy."}]},{"id":"blk-30530","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-39084","text":"Two RFCs, not this document, are the next things to turn into engine code:"}]},{"id":"blk-30531","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-30533","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-39085","marks":["bold"],"text":"`RFC_TRAAVIIS_ARTIFACTS.md`"},{"id":"spn-39086","text":" — the substrate-neutral shared ladder"}]}],"id":"blk-30532","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-30534","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-39087","text":"("},{"id":"spn-39088","marks":["code"],"text":"traaviis.*"},{"id":"spn-39089","text":"): "},{"id":"spn-39090","marks":["code"],"text":"TaskSpecV1"},{"id":"spn-39091","text":", "},{"id":"spn-39092","marks":["code"],"text":"RewardSpecV1"},{"id":"spn-39093","text":", "},{"id":"spn-39094","marks":["code"],"text":"SubstrateProfileV1"},{"id":"spn-39095","text":", "},{"id":"spn-39096","marks":["code"],"text":"EpisodeReceiptV1"},{"id":"spn-39097","text":", and the "},{"id":"spn-39098","marks":["code"],"text":"env-…"},{"id":"spn-39099","text":"/"},{"id":"spn-39100","marks":["code"],"text":"bundle-…"},{"id":"spn-39101","text":"/"},{"id":"spn-39102","marks":["code"],"text":"pack"},{"id":"spn-39103","text":"/"},{"id":"spn-39104","marks":["code"],"text":"serve"},{"id":"spn-39105","text":" surface (the latter marked DEFERRED behind the first environment)."}]},{"id":"blk-30535","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-30537","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-39106","marks":["bold"],"text":"`RFC_EVIDENCE_RESIDENCY.md`"},{"id":"spn-39107","text":" — the first flagship substrate"}]}],"id":"blk-30536","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-30538","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-39108","text":"("},{"id":"spn-39109","marks":["code"],"text":"residency.repository.v1"},{"id":"spn-39110","text":"): "},{"id":"spn-39111","marks":["code"],"text":"SnapshotV1"},{"id":"spn-39112","text":", agent outputs ("},{"id":"spn-39113","marks":["code"],"text":"FindingV1"},{"id":"spn-39114","text":"/"},{"id":"spn-39115","marks":["code"],"text":